From 2d2bd2d2bb98161a527f3de27a799d162c7c42b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:20:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] feat(web): let a page load the local files its
 properties name

Pages load a file or directory property as "file:///" + value, and
Chromium refuses a file: URL to a page of another scheme, so a preset's
own image or video (kept in the preset's folder, not the wallpaper's)
never appeared: the Nezuko presets of 1081733658 showed the visualizer
on black.

The web API shim now maps those URLs to a path under the page's own
scheme, which the scheme handler serves only for a file one of the
properties names, or one directly inside a folder a directory property
names. Paths are made canonical first, so neither ".." nor a symlink
reaches anything else; everything else is refused and logged. Staying
on the page's origin keeps a canvas the file is drawn into readable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tp4kQtVREMqxYupDoiqth6
